<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Egyptian conquest of Kordofan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1821</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Egyptian conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kordofan">Kordofan</a> in 1821 was part of the expansion of Muhammad Ali's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. It removed Kordofan from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>, severing its eastern trade connections and diverting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley commerce, which led to a long economic decline that weakened the sultanate.</p></div>
